\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The analysis of Manhattan Airbnb data reveals clear investment priorities for vacation rental properties. The most attractive neighborhoods, measured by rental frequency via reviews in the last 12 months, are led by Harlem, Hell\'92s Kitchen, and Lower East Side (part of the top 10). Overall, 1-bedroom units dominate popularity with 1,265 listings, followed by 2-bedrooms (526) and studios (441). Neighborhood preferences are consistent: 1-bedroom properties are the clear favorite in Harlem and most top neighborhoods, except Midtown which favors studios. Filtering to these top neighborhoods and their optimal sizes, then ranking by actual 30-day revenue (summed from the calendar sheet and extrapolated to annual estimates by multiplying by 12), highlights the highest-earning listings for maximum ROI.\
These insights directly address the client\'92s need to identify the best property types for investment. By focusing capital on 1-bedroom (and select studio) listings in the top 10 high-review neighborhoods, the client can target proven high-occupancy areas that generate the strongest revenue. The accompanying bar chart of top neighborhoods by reviews, pivot tables showing bedroom preferences, and revenue-ranked listing table provide clear, visual support for these recommendations and reduce investment risk in the competitive Manhattan vacation rental market.\
